# D27 - FMOVE(M) control registers to a PC-relative destination. Both take a
# Line-F; the oracle evaluates the memory-indirect EA first and so marks a
# page descriptor Used.
040 fpuraw/tt seed=963 #543

# D28 - FBcc / FDBcc with an odd displacement on the 68040, taken or not.
# The fork takes the address error inside the branch after evaluating the
# predicate (MC68040UM-1993 §8.2.2, §9.7.1, Table 8-4), stacking the
# branch's address; the oracle sets the PC (or falls through) and never
# raises one.
# On Dirk Hoffmann's core (2026-11-24) none of these raises one either: the
# plain lines below still fail for other reasons — 86 take a Line-F (predicate
# $20-$3F, or reserved FDBcc extension bits), 8 differ on descriptor U bits
# only. The vectors that now agree with the corpus are the @OPEN block below.
