# D28, open defect of the core (TODO.md § Phase 1 › Défauts ouverts du cœur).
# [B] MC68040UM-1993 §8.2.2 (PDF p. 221): "An address error exception occurs
# when the processor attempts to prefetch an instruction from an odd address.
# This includes the case of a conditional branch instruction with an odd
# branch offset that is not taken." Dirk Hoffmann's FBcc/FDBcc (base
# 863b8d02) raise none, taken (14 here) or not (33), as the corpus: these
# vectors agree with it and are counted open.
